Author: Olof Johansson <olof@lixom.net>
Date:   Sun Sep 27 22:47:15 2026 -0700

    discovery: keep a typed gateway port, refuse a bad one

    The manual gateway field parsed host:port and threw the port away, so
    "box:8443" silently loaded box on 443. The gate now keeps the port in
    the origin it returns (443 is the default and is not written), and a
    port that is empty, not a number or outside 1-65535 is refused with
    "Enter a host, or host:port (1–65535)." instead of being dropped. The
    button stays disabled for it; Return shows the reason. Settings ->
    Gateway goes through the same gate.

    The tsnet harness's dash peer also serves tailnet :8443, journaled as
    "dash:8443", so the discovery suite can tell the typed port was used.

    Spec: docs/features/F1-gateway-port.md (manual entry, §2)

