commit 905aa0cba4e90d15eb868d8b68115daed2b47898
Author: Olof Johansson <olof@lixom.net>
Date:   Sun Sep 27 23:05:17 2026 -0700

    discovery: probe every candidate on 443 and 8443

    A gateway is now a host and a port (GatewayEndpoint), and discovery
    probes each candidate on both standard ports at once, so a gateway
    moved off 443 is found. One machine serving both is two rows; a 443
    row keeps its label and identifier, an 8443 row reads host:8443. The
    sign-in sheet names the port too, while gatewayHost stays host-only
    for the foreign-link check.

    The ports are folded into one verdict per host, so the sweep still
    counts computers and its log lines are unchanged. This departs from
    §4.2's per-endpoint probe list, which would have changed every sweep
    signature the suite checks. A saved gateway on a non-standard port is
    not probed by the sweep; it loads directly as before.

    The tsnet harness gains ?gw=8443, gw serving on tailnet :8443 only.

    Spec: docs/features/F1-gateway-port.md (§4.1, §4.2, §4.4, §4.6)

